{"text": "Ethan learns most successfully through visual examples paired with concise explanation; captioned video and transcripts; preview/review of new vocabulary; and small-group discussion with turn-taking. These strategies make instruction clearer and reduce the amount of energy spent simply gaining access.\n\nThe profile also identifies predictable barriers. Ethan may struggle with overlapping talk and background noise; teachers speaking while facing away; uncaptioned media; and listening fatigue late in the day. We should not treat these points as a list of personal deficits. Each one directs the team toward a response. For example, a barrier caused by pace may require additional processing time; an environmental barrier may require a quieter, safer, or more accessible setting; and task complexity may require modeling, chunking, direct instruction, or an alternate response.\n\nThe goal is not to remove every productive challenge. The goal is to remove barriers that prevent the student from engaging with the intended learning. Presenter 3 will now connect the profile’s sensory, medical, behavioural, and safety information to the EA’s day-to-day responsibilities.", "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural", "audio": "special-education-F-04.mp3", "words": [{"text": "Ethan", "start": 0.1, "end": 0.4875, "start_char": 0, "end_char": 5}, {"text": "learns", "start": 0.5, "end": 0.8875, "start_char": 6, "end_char": 12}, {"text": "most", "start": 0.9, "end": 1.1625, "start_char": 13, "end_char": 17}, {"text": "successfully", "start": 1.175, "end": 1.8625, "start_char": 18, "end_char": 30}, {"text": "through", "start": 1.875, "end": 2.1125, "start_char": 31, "end_char": 38}, {"text": "visual", "start": 2.125, "end": 2.475, "start_char": 39, "end_char": 45}, {"text": "examples", "start": 2.4875, "end": 3.0625, "start_char": 46, "end_char": 54}, {"text": "paired", "start": 3.075, "end": 3.4375, "start_char": 55, "end_char": 61}, {"text": "with", "start": 3.45, "end": 3.5875, "start_ch